<title>UK: Cuba 96/97 sugar output could be under 4.2 mln T.</title>
<headline>Cuba 96/97 sugar output could be under 4.2 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cuba could produce no more than 4.2 million tonnes of sugar tel quel in 1996/97, down from 4.45 million the previous year, German statistician F.O. Licht said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Licht cited unidentified Cuban sources for the latest estimate.</p>
<p>&quot;This is likely to support prices, although it was known for quite some time that this year's crop is in difficulties,&quot; Licht said in its daily report.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
